*Procedure to Remove Saved GitHub Credentials in Windows*
Step 1: Open Control Panel
Press Windows + S.
Type Control Panel.
Click to open it.
Step 2: Open Credential Manager
Click User Accounts.
Select Credential Manager.
Click Windows Credentials.
Step 3: Find GitHub Credentials
Scroll down to Generic Credentials.
Look for an entry named git:https://github.com or another entry related to GitHub.


Step 4: Remove the Credentials
Click the GitHub-related entry to expand it.
Click Remove.
Click Yes to confirm.
Step 5: Verify
Open VS Code.
Open the terminal.
Run: git push
4. If authentication is requested, sign in using your own GitHub account.
Important: This removes the saved GitHub login credential from Windows. It does not delete the GitHub account or any repositories.



